They always do that.  More precisely, the mysterious force will only
send monsters back one level, and if the monster is hurt, it'll
teleport to the upstairs as soon as you enter the level.

But I wouldn't do this with Rodney if I had a choice.  Much better to
leave a named demon alive for this purpose.  Asmodeus is particularly
convenient, being essentially harmless to cold resistant characters.

(Fleeing monsters also won't climb up the stairs from the Valley to
the Castle.  This has to do with the fact that, to the game code,
those aren't normal stairs but special inter-branch ones.  They will
follow _you_ up even those stairs, though.)

